:: Carter Hero's Weakness Part 2 [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 10>>
<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> quickly explains the game, setting up his bedroom as the final boss room. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“The villain is Alternate Ultraman!”</span> <span style="color:Pink">He holds up an adorable stuffed bear dressed in Ultraman attire with a scarf with a sewn frowny face wrapped around its mouth. You comment on the cute stuffed friend and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> chuckles shyly,</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It’s an old toy I’ve had since I was a baby. Normally, I’d see it as a collectable, but since it is already so old, I don’t mind playing with it. But he’s playing his evil alter-ego today. He makes a good villain since he has the same powers as Ultraman, but a heart of evil! He’s from an alternate universe where everything is opposite and”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> goes on a bit of a rant, <span style="color:Pink">though it is rather cute as he explains detailed comic book lore until he realizes how long he has been going and pauses with a chuckle.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Sorry, got a bit distracted for a second there.”</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },
                },
            {
                Name: "Carter",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Everyday",
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
        ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

The two of you head out into his yard to start the game when suddenly <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> realizes he is forgetting a super important piece! <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh! We have to decide your superhero identity. I already have mine, Ultraboy!”</span> <span style="color:Pink">He smiles as he does a cute pose, causing you to laugh and ask if that isn’t a little on the nose.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“No! It’s cool. I’m a superfan that wasn’t born with powers but wear special clothes that give me powers just like Ultraman.”</span> He points to his $CarterTop.Name and smiles, showing it off as the pretend source of his powers, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Getting my powers from my clothes means I’m not weak to the same stuff as Ultraman, though do have my own weaknesses.”</span> He laughs. It’s pretty obvious what the flaw in his powerset is. <span style="color:Pink">If his powers come from his clothing, then all you need to do to remove his powers is-</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But what about your powers? Got any in mind?”</span> He asks, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“We can say this is your first mission, which is why you don’t have a costume or name yet, but we gotta figure out your power set! Anything in mind?”</span> <span style="color:Yellow">You think for a moment, trying to come up with a powerset that fits you.</span> <br>
<br>

<div id="choice">
	<<link "Super speed<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        <span style="color:LightGreen">After a moment of thinking, you decide on super speed!</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Nice, kinda like The Blur! He’s super cool. He moves so fast he can like shoot lightning and stuff!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> does a bit of a different heroic pose, looking like he is running in place. <span style="color:LightGreen">You piece together that this must be the signature pose of this speedster and try to mimic it, feeling a bit silly but finding it charming.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Alright! Let’s go!”</span> <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                    {
                        Name: "Player",
                        State: {
                            Mouth: "Happy",
                            Eyes: "Mad",
                        },
                        },
                    {
                        Name: "Carter",
                        State: {
                            Outfit: "Everyday",
                            Mouth: "Happy",
                            Eyes: "Mad",
                        },
                    },
                ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        The battle scene is set: about two dozen of Alternate Ultraman’s goons stand between you and his base of operations, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s house. Ultraboy goes in first, rushing over at high speeds and delivering a devastating punch to the air, the shockwave enough to send a horde of goons flying! He then rushes in and begins to brawl with the group, swinging his fists and ducking under their blows. He is clearly an expert at this. <br>
        <br>
        Meanwhile, you use your own powers to your advantage! You rush in at super speed, moving from one to the other and delivering a series of 8 punches within a single second, the force powerful enough to knock each of the goons out cold! You then see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> in need of aid and rush over, racing around him as face as you can to generate a blast of lightning that sends the final goon into the pool with an electric splash! <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Thanks! Your powers are quite electrifying, haha!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> says in a cute, mature voice, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You’ll fit right into my group of superfriends!”</span> <span style="color:LightGreen">You internally roll your eyes, but follow along as the two of you manage to slip inside the evil base.</span> <br>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Carter Hero's Weakness Part 3]]<br>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
	<<link "Telekinesis<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        <span style="color:LightGreen">After a moment of thinking, you decide on telekinesis!</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Cool! Moving stuff with your mind is super fun! Ultraman has a friend named Alien that can do that. Not a creative name, but he’s super cool, even if he isn’t that popular anymore.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> does a rather interesting pose that looks a bit mysterious and dark, which you piece together must be an iconic pose of this more mysterious, uncreatively named hero. <span style="color:LightGreen">You try to mimic the pose, feeling a bit silly, but finding it very charming.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Alright! Let’s go!”</span> <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                    {
                        Name: "Player",
                        State: {
                            Mouth: "Happy",
                            Eyes: "Mad",
                        },
                        },
                    {
                        Name: "Carter",
                        State: {
                            Outfit: "Everyday",
                            Mouth: "Happy",
                            Eyes: "Mad",
                        },
                    },
                ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        The battle scene is set: about two dozen of Alternate Ultraman’s goons stand between you and his base of operations, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s house. Ultraboy goes in first, rushing over at high speeds and delivering a devastating punch to the air, the shockwave enough to send a horde of goons flying! He then rushes in and begins to brawl with the group, swinging his fists and ducking under their blows. He is clearly an expert at this. <br>
        <br>
        Meanwhile, you use your own powers to your advantage! You use the various outdoor furniture and lift them up with your mind, throwing it at the group of enemies and using the very world around them as your weapon. A barbeque pins one against the wall, another is assaulted by pool noodles, the final one has his own clothes turn against him as you use them to send him flying into a pool with a devasting splash! <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Nice work! You have great control over your powers!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> says in a cute, mature voice, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You’ll fit right into my group of superfriends!”</span> <span style="color:LightGreen">You internally roll your eyes, but follow along as the two of you manage to slip inside the evil base.</span> <br>
        <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Carter Hero's Weakness Part 3]]<br>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
	<<link "Fire powers<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        <span style="color:LightGreen">After a moment of thinking, you decide on having fire powers!</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Awesome! Fire powers are super cool, you can burn stuff and use them to attack or defend. It’s very powerful! So many heroes use them, so it can be hard to stand out sometimes, but I bet you’ll be the coolest fire hero!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> does a pose with his arms at his size, as if he is blasting out a bolt of fire. <span style="color:LightGreen">It is probably a pose often seen with these types of heroes and you do your best to mimic it, feeling a bit silly, but finding it very charming.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Alright! Let’s go!”</span> <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                    {
                        Name: "Player",
                        State: {
                            Mouth: "Smirk",
                            Eyes: "Mad",
                        },
                        },
                    {
                        Name: "Carter",
                        State: {
                            Outfit: "Everyday",
                            Mouth: "Happy",
                            Eyes: "Mad",
                        },
                    },
                ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        The battle scene is set: about two dozen of Alternate Ultraman’s goons stand between you and his base of operations, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s house. Ultraboy goes in first, rushing over at high speeds and delivering a devastating punch to the air, the shockwave enough to send a horde of goons flying! He then rushes in and begins to brawl with the group, swinging his fists and ducking under their blows. He is clearly an expert at this. <br>
        <br>
        Meanwhile, you use your own powers to your advantage! You unleash an inferno at the horde, smirking as they scream and try to rush into the pool to put out the fires. Your flames grant you complete control over the battlefield, as none can even get close to you without feeling the heat and you are quickly able to scare the remaining goons off. You laugh as you blast a fireball into the pool, heating it enough to send those that jumped in there fleeing from the boiling water. <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Not bad, though try to keep the collateral damage to a minimum, hot head.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> says in a cute, mature voice. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Remember, if you want to be part of my superfriends, you have to be a hero first!”</span> <span style="color:LightGreen">You internally roll your eyes, but follow along as the two of you manage to slip inside the evil base.</span> <br>
        <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Carter Hero's Weakness Part 3]]<br>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
</div>